					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-21 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>And here we are sitting through another Tuesday.<br />
<br />
Tomorrow night is the big night.&nbsp; By the time you read this, the <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> show at the Showbox, November 22nd, will be sold out, cuzzo.<br />
<br />
In other music related news, check out the new feature on the site!&nbsp; In
the upper right corner of your browser, there&#39;s a flash image of a
graphic equalizer and a link directly beneath it.&nbsp; This link is the
&quot;free weekly mp3,&quot; or at least, it will be until we think of a more
cutting edge name for it.&nbsp; The downloads will be anything from
unreleased MassLine material, to mixtape tracks, to maybe just good
Seattle music that we think you need to get hip to.<br />
<br />
We&#39;re currently featuring <strong>Blue Scholars - Inkwell (Crashed Cop Car Remix)</strong> since we&#39;re still getting a bunch of requests for it.<br />
<br />
If you have any particular interests as far as what music should be available
for download, then don&#39;t be a sukka and just think it!&nbsp; Go post your ideas in the forum!<br />
<br />
Thas thas whassup.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-20 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><span style="display: inline"><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/m3GstYOIc0I"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/m3GstYOIc0I"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object><br /><br /></span><span class="body1 style73"><span style="display: inline">Iranian-American,
U.S. CITIZEN and UCLA student, Mostafa Tabatabainejad, was shot by
UCLA&#39;S UCPD November 14th 2006, because he could not show his Student
ID. He was shot 5 times with a taser gun. Police threatened to shoot
students who got too close. The Student yelled out that he had a
medical condition, but the cops kept shooting. </span></span><span style="display: inline"><br /><br />Somebody caught the whole ordeal on their camera phone.</span><span style="display: inline">  <a href="http://dailybruin.com/news/articles.asp?id=38960"><strong>The Daily Bruin</strong></a> wrote an article about it, and <a href="http://www.mideastyouth.com/?p=547"><strong>MideastYouth.com</strong></a> also has something about the incident.<br /><br />Let us know what you think.<br /><br /><br />Saba<br /></span><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-19 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>&quot;<strong>Hip Hop: Back To It&#39;s Roots</strong>&quot; was in Seattle this weekend, a play written &amp; directed by <strong>Melissa Noelle-Greene</strong> complete with workshops at the <strong>Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center</strong>... feauturing none other then <strong>Davey D </strong>of <strong><a href="http://www.myspace.com/mrdaveyd">Hard-Knock Radio</a></strong>.  word is they had a press conference with <strong>Talib Kweli</strong> and <strong>survivors of Hurricane Katrina </strong>who are now living in the Northwest.  if anyone out there made it out to this event, let us know how it went in <a href="http://www.masslinemedia.com/smf">the forums</a>.<br /><br />On the subject of Hurricane Katrina, our sista <strong>Walidah Imarisha</strong> put together an amazing documentary on the subject called &quot;<strong>Finding Common Ground in New Orleans</strong>&quot; you can find more information on this subject off her <a href="http://www.myspace.com/channelzeromedia">myspace site</a> and the film is being distributed by <a href="http://www.twn.org"><strong>Third World Newsreel</strong></a>.<br /><br />I also wanted to give a shout-out to the homies <strong>Asun</strong> &amp; <strong>Jerm</strong> of <a href="http://www.myspace.com/1stplatoon"><strong>Alpha-P</strong></a> who are wrapping up a tour tonight in Las Vegas with <strong>Himself</strong>, and <strong>Sleep</strong> of Oldominion at the <a href="http://www.myspace.com/sundayskoolin"><strong>Sunday Skoolin&#39;</strong></a>.<br /><br />and on a more personal note, i finished a mix-tape last week entitled &quot;<strong>Westlake: Class Of 1999</strong>&quot;... 22 tracks recorded in 3 citys over the last 4 years that never had a home... juss a lil somethin&#39; to hold you over till the national release of <strong>Lovework</strong> coming February &#39;07.  you can get more details and order the mixtape off <a href="http://www.myspace.com/gabrielteodros">myspace.com/gabrielteodros</a><br /><br />Now go catch Talib Kweli and Buckshot at the Showbox, tonight at 8pm.  let us know how it goes.......<br /><br />-- gt<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-18 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>four thumbs down for 4pm sunsets.  the inhabitants of the northwest are patiently waiting for the sun to return so we can live normal lives again that don&#39;t involve crippling depression...<br /><br />but on a lighter note!  <br /><br />today is ultimate sportsfan day. if i wasn&#39;t havin dinner with my mom, i&#39;d probably be in the soufend watching the pacquiao/morales fight.  one of the most anticipated matchups of the year.<br /><br />grab a san pelligrino, some hummus, and embrace the animalistic side of your human nature by watching two men beat each other senseless.<br /><br /><br />howla.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-16 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>for all thugs with a heart, <strong>Lyfe Jennings</strong> is performing tonight at the Showbox.  assuming i can get all my work done for the day, i&#39;ll be there for shure.<br /><br />speaking of things that are filthy, check it out...<br /><br />the new Artist Handstyle Tee is HERE!<br /><br /><img src="../images/peekpreview.jpg" alt="" width="430" height="241" align="middle" /><br /><br />this month&#39;s shirt is brought to you by <strong>peekaboo!</strong><br />from Seattle, WA and the Islamic Republic of Iran. you may have seen<br />peekaboo!&#39;s art at shows, on shoes, skateboards around the town...<br />shooooot, you&#39;ve likely seen something of his somewhere! i mean, the<br />young man&#39;s been playing with himself since 1983.<br /><br />he reps a crew called <a href="http://www.myspace.com/pocketfullofmonsters">Pocket Full Of Monsters</a>.<br />if you like their work--which we certainly do--you&#39;re in luck because<br />peeks is just the first of this camp to represent on MassLine cloth. <br /><br />these items will be available <strong>FIRST</strong> at the <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> show, <strong>November 22nd</strong> at the <strong>Showbox</strong>.<br /><br />speaking of the ThingsTaken show, one of the opening acts, OneSelf, was written about in the Stranger.  check &#39;em out <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=104379" target="_blank">here</a>.<br /><br />til next time,<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> [56] <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
